course: dictionary
lesson: 15279
title: Simplification
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: A simplification is the act of making something simpler or easier to understand or do. It comes from the word simple. «The map was a simplification of the city, with only the main roads drawn.»
explain: A simplification can be very useful, because it helps you learn the main idea first. But it can also leave out details. Saying «an atom is like a tiny ball» is a useful simplification, but real atoms are more complicated than that.
explain: When someone says «that is an oversimplification», they mean the simple version has gone too far and is no longer quite right. «Saying all birds can fly is an oversimplification, because penguins cannot.»
explain: In maths, simplification means making a fraction or expression simpler without changing its value. Simplifying 4/8 gives 1/2, and both show the same amount.
fact: Simplification is a noun: one simplification, many simplifications.
fact: «Simplification» means making something simpler or easier to understand or do.
fact: «Oversimplification» means a simplification that leaves out so much it is no longer quite right.
fact: In maths, «simplification» means making a fraction simpler, like 4/8 becoming 1/2.
fact: A useful simplification helps you learn the main idea first, and the details can come later.
exercise: «The teacher's chart was a simplification of the plant's life cycle, with only five stages.» What is a simplification? | *Making something simpler to understand | A long and detailed report | A type of plant | Making something harder on purpose
exercise: «Saying all birds can fly is an oversimplification, because penguins cannot.» What does oversimplification suggest? | *The simple idea has gone too far and is not quite right | The idea is perfectly correct and complete | The idea is very long | The idea is a fact about penguins
exercise: In maths, what does simplification of a fraction mean? | Changing its value to something new | *Making it simpler without changing its value | Making it bigger | Adding a whole number to it
test: Which sentence uses «simplification» correctly? | The simplification of the city was a long, detailed photograph. | *The map was a useful simplification of the city, showing only the main roads. | A simplification is the name of a fish. | Simplification means losing your temper.
test: Why might a teacher give a simplification? | To leave the idea out completely | *To make a hard idea easier to understand at first | To make the class longer | To make the idea harder to understand
exam: What does «an oversimplification» mean? | *A simple explanation that has left out so much it is no longer quite right | A word for a very simple sum | A very long and detailed explanation | A mistake in a maths test
